feat(kebab): apply a slide to the pre-mapped dyld shared cache

The split cache is built for a slide below maxSlide: four mappings (the
__DATA_CONST and __DATA ranges of the two .dylddata subcaches) carry
dyld slide-info v2, and every address in the cache files is unslid.  The
pre-mapped path set VM_PROT_SLIDE nowhere and left srfmp->slide at zero,
so a dyld that found a non-zero cache base could not have rebased the
data pages.

Consume dyld_cache_mapping_and_slide_info and cross-check it against each
subcache's mapping table.  Locate the slide-info blob in the trailing r--
mapping of the same file, then validate the v2 header, 4 KiB page size,
page count against the mapping size, table bounds, and the 64-bit delta
mask before anything is mapped.

Add kebab_dsc_slide=<bytes> (default 0) to force a slide.  Reject a value
that is not 16 KiB aligned, is not below maxSlide, or pushes a mapping or
a slide-info blob outside the arm64 shared region.  For a non-zero slide,
shift every mapping and every sms_slide_start, set VM_PROT_SLIDE on the
four mappings that carry slide info, and pass the same value in
srfmp->slide so the lazy pager's sr_slide and the base that
shared_region_check_np() returns to dyld agree.  Slide 0 keeps the
previous unslid path.

Extend scripts/check-shared-cache.py with --slide so the host plan and the
kernel plan can be compared on the real 44 files, with the same alignment,
maxSlide and shared-region checks.  The real cache has 51 mappings, four
of them slid, and .27.dylddata mapping 1 is the first to relocate.
